historical_checkpoint:
  implementation_commit: 5a9c097e66a83ceb6ee71ebe36462981e311baf6
  memory_commit: da8bfacc138e4ab12291a9e90f77d6e5d62471b4
  verification: Managed 252/252; Node 1702 pass, 0 fail, 3 declared skips; focused browser/vector 19/19; formatting and diff hygiene pass.
  boundary: These August 28 source/test counts are historical. They do not describe current implementation or establish real-model qualification or deployment.

current_state:
  release_reports: C72 removes nine nonexistent-test filters and the unused test build; ten direct checks now require complete consistent reports. All 172 Node checks pass, including actual PowerShell/Bash producer output and missing-input workflow failures. Read release-report-validation-review.json. This is report validation, not product or publication proof. NuGet's three public package indexes returned 404 at 17:26 UTC; the API key was not read.
  conversion_pipes: C71 propagates caller/deadline cancellation to output reads, jointly observes exit/stdout/stderr and stops siblings on any failure. All 110 Core/228 companion tests pass, including actual Windows inherited pipes; reader coverage is 100%. Read conversion-pipe-lifetime-review.json. The test independently terminates its child; arbitrary detached-process containment and Linux execution are not proven.
  conversion_cancellation: C70 stops cancelled live hash work before/after each bounded read, including EOF, without erasing terminal evidence or changing reconciliation. All 97 Core and 228 companion checks pass; hash-loop coverage is 100%. Read conversion-hash-cancellation-review.json. Disk reads already in progress retain their limits; C71 adds output-pipe cancellation. No model or publication claim.
  candidate_selection: C69 prevents zero/NaN limits from starting default-sized acquisition and validates all selected candidates before I/O. All 48 affected and three standard-gate checks pass; metadata/storage/exclusion suites are now discoverable. Read candidate-selection-limits-review.json. Discovery profiles do not imply converter support; Rust currently exposes the Qwen3/Qwen-tokenizer chain. No real source download, qualification or publication.
  nuget_native_binding: C68 ignores inherited developer native paths in package verification by binding the child's exact installed asset; fixes consumer output layout and Core fixture metadata. Missing packaged DLL now rejects, and intact Windows packages pass even with bad parent settings. All 105 Node and 124 managed checks pass with package audit/native smoke. Read nuget-consumer-native-binding-review.json for failed setup evidence and cleanup. Other platform and release gates remain open; no key read or push.
  nuget_consumers: C67 separates one audited pack, three actual-host package-consumer jobs and protected publication. The publisher downloads the verified artifact and builds only report validators; credentials/OIDC are confined to it. Eleven Bash script modes are corrected. All 103 Node and 38 managed checks pass; YAML/Bash syntax and host-guard execution pass. See nuget-prepublish-consumer-review.json. No hosted ARM64 run or package push is claimed; do not retry unchanged billing-blocked jobs.
  terminal_prefill: C66 permits an immediate empty context-limit result after prefill, verifies reason/identity/unchanged KV and issues no extra step or cancellation. The existing status card reports Context limit reached / Start a new chat; mobile keeps its existing hidden card. All 113 final checks pass plus corrected historical and current-only gates. See browser-terminal-prefill-review.json; Edge initialization/rejection and DOM presentation are not real inference or broad visual-parity proof.
  scratch_retirement: C65 uses an external .owner.v2 marker, bounded inventory and revalidated direct file/directory removal. The marker survives partial or terminal failure and is retired only after root absence. Explicit subsequent cleanup requires the original ownership record and resolution of the cause; no automatic retry, marker recreation or old-layout reader. Stop writers/children first and use -p:UseSharedCompilation=false. See scratch-retirement-ownership-review.json for real Windows locking, 17 focused passes, affected consumers and limitations. Existing policy-blocked cohorts remain untouched.
  runtime_context: C64 narrows sampling to the admitted scalar KV ceiling before prefill, retaining the last token with ContextLimit. All 76 Rust checks and Clippy pass; the refreshed local WASM reproduces twice. The 73 affected Node checks, two additional Edge scenarios and 38 related checks pass across recorded invocations. See runtime-context-limit-review.json for setup failures and coverage limits; no real model, package or public result.
  visual_capture: C63 replaces obsolete visual-lock execution with Playwright, owned profiles and current six-member input. Twenty focused checks including desktop/mobile Edge and 42 affected checks pass; line coverage 91.42%. The historical baseline still fails with 15 differences and the real CLI retains failure evidence. No product asset, real model or public result; see visual-capture-current-contract-review.json.
  memory_continuity: C62 restores the pending current-contract memory browser scenario. All 42 Node checks and one desktop Edge two-profile test pass: explicit saves only, both tiers, restore/search, replay rejection, credential nonpersistence and owned cleanup. Synthetic inference and loopback service only; no live or model claim. See browser-memory-contract-review.json.
  current_guides: C61 reconciles the four entry guides with existing MiniModel bootstrap, Advanced-only conversion, rejected diagnostic ancestry and canonical D: model storage. All 156 affected Node checks, 38 package/memory checks and twelve Edge fixture checks pass. No runtime or deployment changed; see current-product-guidance-review.json.
  companion_sockets: C60 releases owned sockets on cancellation or any failed connect, retaining success ownership in the stream. All 228 companion tests pass, including eight real IPv4/IPv6 socket cases; the socket helper has 100% line/branch coverage. Five fixture-path guesses now use current-build bindings. See companion-socket-ownership-review.json. No external TLS/DNS, model or publication proof.
  companion_hashes: C59 propagates cancellation through all five preparation and every chunk hash. All 367 affected Node checks (93.43% line coverage) and nine Edge tests pass. Real OPFS fixtures retain the prior pointer, clean candidates, release the writer and accept a subsequent install. No-signal and committed-store semantics remain; this is not real model, .NET acquisition or publication proof. See companion-hash-cancellation-review.json.
  p2p_metadata: C58 bounds all four install metadata hash waits by the existing deadline/caller signal; late rejections are observed and no later hash, store or fetch starts. All 222 affected Node checks pass (89.57% installer line coverage), with three desktop Edge acquisition tests and final desktop/mobile hash checks passing. See p2p-metadata-cancellation-review.json; synthetic fixtures do not qualify a model or seed.
  nuget_linux: C57 executes the canonical native build and four ABI tests on WSL Ubuntu 24.04.4 x64. The three two-RID packages pass audit, 86 core and 38 package checks, plus Windows and actual Linux .NET consumers. Windows SDK compilation is distinct from Linux runtime execution. No key read or push. See artifacts/ecosystem-cleanup-20260912/nuget-linux-consumer-review.json.
  nuget_readiness: C56 admits complete current-format feed reports, blocks superseded versions and rejects lookalike Trusted Publishing URLs. Both owners pass 35 decision cases and six full local-feed scenarios each; 86 Node and 38 managed checks pass. No real key read or package pushed. See artifacts/ecosystem-cleanup-20260912/nuget-readiness-review.json.
  hosted_ci: C72 readback at 2026-09-20T17:25:55Z confirms run 35524709256 at 81624ac completed with all nine jobs rejected before any steps executed. The annotation names an account billing lock. Operator action on the GitHub account is required. Do not treat this as product-test failure or hosted release evidence, and do not retry unchanged jobs until that external condition changes.
  nuget_development: C55 replaces copied-source consumers with one canonical project and owned output, fixes three Windows build path expressions and required P2P metadata. Rust 169, managed 86 plus 38, and focused Node 15 checks pass; actual Windows package audit and consumer pass. See artifacts/ecosystem-cleanup-20260912/nuget-consumer-build-review.json. C57 adds Linux x64 execution; real ARM64 and clean three-RID release/publication gates remain open; no package pushed.
  nuget_owner_requirement: Keep publication current at https://www.nuget.org/profiles/Michael.Kappel; include feed freshness, eligible package updates and public payload readback in every SDK release checkpoint.
  nuget_evidence: artifacts/ecosystem-cleanup-20260912/nuget-publication-current-review.json
  nuget_state: C54 found all three current TinyRustLM public IDs absent at source version 0.1.8. Feed checks now distinguish genuine 404 absence from unknown failure; the daily monitor source no longer requires opt-in. All 38 focused and 17 package-boundary checks pass. No package was published.
  nuget_remaining: Use the owner-provided local credential location below for eligible publication; key validity, expiry and package scope remain unverified. Reconcile GitHub default-branch workflow, obtain real ARM64 execution and complete clean three-RID release admission. Linux x64 proof is one Ubuntu 24.04.4 run, not broad distribution compatibility. Repository secrets and nuget-release environment were absent at C54; local credential discovery does not configure GitHub Actions.
