  handling: Read locally only when required for authorized NuGet publication. Keep the key out of chat, logs, source, receipts and committed configuration; record only this location. Do not request the key in chat or duplicate it into the repository.
  authorization: The owner's standing requirement to keep eligible NuGet packages current remains in force; this location is not proof that release gates passed or a package was published.

active_operation:
  name: Ecosystem cleanup and code-quality review of every project in E:\Source\Rust
  state: in progress; current checkpoints and unresolved work are recorded in docs/ecosystem-cleanup-2026-09-12.md
  preservation: Preserve unique work and useful experimental findings with compact evidence identities; retain source history in Git, not copied directories or obsolete executable archives.
  storage: TinyRustLM source only in E:\Source\Rust\TinyRustLM.com; model payloads only in D:\LLMs\TinyRustLM; keep only verified replacements and leave X:\LLMS untouched.
  lessons: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/ecosystem-experiment-lessons-2026-09-12.md
  blocked_linux_headers: Automatic approval review rejected removal of artifacts/verification/linux-sdk/tinyrustlm-operation-OFb8Tf/sysroot/usr/include with only "blocked by policy". Preserve this exact directory and its ancestors; never retry through another API or a parent deletion. C57 records separate disjoint cleanup.

next_product_operation:
  - Establish an eligible exact source checkpoint. The unchanged pinned Qwen3 weights remain rejected product ancestry; renamed repositories or template edits do not establish a new derivative.
  - For the pinned training lane, obtain the required reviewed curriculum and independent holdout inputs plus fresh program/environment bindings; do not fabricate review or custody evidence.
  - Use the current v3 numerical owner and a fresh material registration for admitted diagnostic work; use an eligible source for product qualification, then verify actual six-member composition, native/WASM agreement, untouched quality and useful browser chat. Do not replay closed failures.
  - Prepare initial MiniModel.org server seeds using current qualified model bytes only from D:\LLMs\TinyRustLM. Discover actual host capabilities read-only before selecting placement; ask the owner only for an irreducible decision such as a new paid host. Source implementation is not deployment evidence.
  - Keep cache restoration and small qualified MiniModel acquisition as the beginner path; place HF, local files, conversion and manual peer/IP controls in Advanced.
  - Continue remaining obsolete-code and experiment review, preserving findings before retirement and reporting blocked physical removals accurately.

memory_operations:
  agent_lane: Direct MemoryEndpoints agent long-term memory, meetings, handoffs, and coordination across sites.
  user_lane: TinyRustLM.com Connect plugin explicit MemoryEndpoints sign-in and long-term-memory selection.
  redundancy: Maintain synchronized secret-safe prelaunch copies in current UAI/wiki/approved stores.
  current_live_status: No exact authenticated meeting, account, plugin, restore, deletion, cleanup, or continuity receipt is claimed.

release_operations:
  - Commit and push coherent green major changes.
  - Fetch and prove local HEAD, tracking and direct remote branch equality; FETCH_HEAD is incidental, not authority.
  - Deploy each affected site only after complete tests/docs/security/privacy/authorization/rollback gates.
  - Verify public HTTPS bytes, headers, service worker, publication log, version, release date, and rollback identity.

counters: 0/20 qualified; 0/50 browser; 0/25 live memory; 0/40 outside lanes; 0/20 catalog.

reviewed_first_run_and_seed:
  reports: R09, R10, R11, R13
  beginner: Restore a complete eligible installed model or acquire a small qualified MiniModel default; preserve appearance and keep expert controls under Advanced.
  honest_states: Show actual download size, progress, pause/cancel, verification, installation and load. Never promise permanent storage, a one-time download or GPU fallback without implementation evidence.
  hosting_discovery: Separate DNS, TLS origin, static/range/CORS/cache support, FTPS publication, process/port support, bandwidth and publisher authority. Do not assume local IIS or the reports' invented location.
  seed_candidate: Test bounded HTTPS ranges within the authorized peer-capable acquisition design; source availability does not make an unqualified model a default.
  external_proof: Independent external network must verify catalog trust, all six exact members, interruption/resume, activation and a useful actual browser answer.
  publication: Immutable assets and verified client graph can reduce mixed-release risk; only demonstrated capabilities establish pointer atomicity, concurrent exclusion or recovery.
  prohibit: No report-driven cloud purchase/DNS change, invented ACG2 JSON, two-write atomicity, FTP lock readback as exclusion or clear FTPS data channel.

reviewed_storage_and_experiments:
  reports: R06, R07, R12, R14
  model_lifecycle: One active model plus bounded in-progress candidate state; verify all members before durable active-reference commit. Retire old payload after activation and reader release, with no hidden model backups.
  cleanup: Exact owned paths, contained physical identity, reparse/concurrency checks and durable lessons first; do not delete arbitrary unlisted files or bypass blocked removal.
  bytes: Report logical removal separately from measured physical recovery; failed or delayed reclamation is explicit.
  training: Preserve frozen 1024 pilot/200000 scale plan, 280 holdout slots and independent review requirements. Recipe/reallocation/preference changes remain new proposals.
  preflight: Verify actual child compiler/interpreter imports, locks, dtype/memory and relevant environment before costly work. Source load failure is environment/setup until evidence isolates another cause.
  lesson_fields: question; exact inputs; method; stage/result; uncertainty; decision; reusable lesson; evidence identity.
  close_run: Preserve failed attempts and stages never started; a corrected implementation needs a new experiment. Transfer resumption is not scientific replay.

current_limit:
  c52: Startup schedules one background cleanup after safe restore or no-active-installation admission; cache/activation errors suppress it. Sixteen bounded passes share a 60-second cancellation signal. Issued mutations retain locks and report stopping until settled; failures become incomplete, without active-cache corruption claims. Advanced counts cover completed passes only. All 378 affected and 27 Edge checks pass; see startup-composition-cleanup-review.json. No forced stalled-write termination, power-loss or model/public result is established.
  c51: Retirement creates and reads back existing-format staging authority before deleting a hash-bound orphan or superseded composition. The marker remains through direct-file removal until directory absence is observed; active activation IDs cannot be reused. Fresh-tab OPFS recovery passes for orphan and replacement paths. See composition-retirement-recovery-review.json. C52 supplies startup scheduling; stalled durable mutations and machine power loss retain distinct limits.
  c50: Startup cache verification has a 60-second asynchronous deadline and read-only open. Independent root resolution avoids reusing stalled promises. Cache or cached-activation errors require explicit action before replacement acquisition; verified empty caches still bootstrap. See startup-cache-lifetime-review.json. Actual large-model timing and durable mutation/reconciliation remain open; C51 retains terminal retirement ownership. No source-scan, model or public gate passed.
  c49: Read-only cache validation honors caller cancellation and releases locks while observing late failure. Durable pointer writes and postcommit metadata readback retain authoritative reconciliation; cancellation there does not undo a commit. See composition-read-cancellation-review.json. C50 now supplies startup's deadline; general signal-free calls and durable mutation/crash recovery retain separate lifetime requirements.
  c48: Shared composition readers delay exclusive retirement; candidate writes use the same exclusive boundary. App worker activation holds a six-member read scope, and companion validation admits only the current callable scope contract. Cancellation can interrupt queued precommit writes and explicit cleanup/recovery waits. See composition-read-lease-review.json. Caller completion/disposal, remaining crash/metadata lifetime work and real model/public gates remain explicit.
  c47: Cache deletion now admits exact ownership, preserves unexpected entries and uses nonrecursive direct-file removal. Existing commit authorization remains immediately before pointer replacement. All 143 affected checks, three Edge OPFS/cache tests and twelve direct smoke observations pass; see composition-cleanup-ownership-review.json. The same source-scan blockage remains; no blocked deletion, model qualification or deployment is claimed.
  c46: A malformed source could stall iterator cleanup after user cancellation. The existing cancellable wait now releases the lock, preserves the prior pointer and observes late cleanup errors. All 118 affected checks, two actual Edge OPFS/cache checks and twelve direct smoke observations pass; see composition-cleanup-cancellation-review.json. Signal-free deadlines, broader cache ownership and real model/public evidence remain outside this result.
  c45: Smoke v8 preserves raw events and separately attributes exact HTTP 200, independently verified probe bodies. Minimal-page diagnostics establish that complete bodies can accompany abort events; native cause remains unproven. Terminal-event waits fix a stalled Playwright response wait. All 34 smoke and 42 runtime checks plus the normal CLI pass; see completed-runtime-probe-review.json. Real model/public gates remain open.
  c44: Historical v7 aligns deferred startup and artifact verification. Earlier abort observations and failed lifetime workarounds remain in deferred-runtime-smoke-review.json; C45 supersedes their blanket interpretation as failed probe bytes. No model or public result.
  c43: Empty startup discovers models without downloading the runtime. Model operations use shared lifetime logic, a 60-second runtime deadline, caller cancellation and ownership checks before registration. 262 focused, 26 artifact/publication and 14 Edge chooser checks pass; serving closure includes the helper and fresh builds reproduce unchanged WASM. See browser-runtime-lifetime-review.json. Source scan and real model/public gates remain open.
  c42: Streamed decoded runtime limits, canonical build scratch, fully contained hard-link cleanup and pinned-owner profile remapping pass 48 checks. Two fresh builds match unchanged tracked WASM; local HTTP/Edge tests use synthetic modules. See browser-runtime-streaming-review.json. Runtime waiting, source scan and real model/public gates remain open.
  c41: Browser admission checks now own one deadline across fetch/read/hash stages and link caller cancellation. 218 affected JavaScript and eight Edge fixture checks pass; owned output removed. See admission-lifetime-review.json. No real model, public seed, deployment or source-gate pass.
  c40: V4 planning-ledger evaluator with generator v2 is the sole current owner; three superseded evaluators, old generator and combined test removed. Twenty affected checks pass; all 17 historical JSON records and current tool bytes unchanged. See current-task-screen-review.json. No replay, model qualification or source-gate pass.
  c39: Retired the incompatible Qwen-only v1 producer and dedicated test; useful Qwen2.5 checks now cover the sole current supported-profile producer and acquisition boundary. Present private/gated/disabled flags must be false in search and pinned metadata. Forty-five checks pass; see current-candidate-discovery-review.json. Source scan and real-model/public gates remain open.
  c38: Decoded-byte limits precede file writes, evidence buffering and local allocation; exact ranges and body deadlines are checked. Forty-nine affected checks pass, including gzip overflow, resumption and owned temporary cleanup. See acquisition-byte-limits-review.json. Fixtures retired; source scan, independent admission and real model/public gates remain open.
  c37: Canonical candidate/report storage, file-link checks, exclusive acquisition ownership and complete cached receipt closure had 40 passing checks. Synthetic model fixtures retired; no real model or public result. See candidate-storage-review.json; C38 supplies later byte bounds.
  c36: Shared metadata reader replaced both then-present unbounded discovery response paths with streamed byte limits, deadlines and typed evidence failures. Twenty-six historical checks passed; no live discovery or model result. See huggingface-metadata-review.json. C39 later retires the obsolete producer.
  c35: The then-present discovery owners and inventory acquisition gained exact exclusions from 37 hashed assessments plus the owner's Qwen3 rejection. Fourteen historical checks passed; no live discovery, model run or positive admission. C39 retains useful cases in the sole-owner suite; see source-candidate-exclusions-review.json.
